# Kanban workflow (mandatory)

All agent work is processed through the **Kanban Markdown** board (`.devtool/features/`).  
Read [docs/agent/KANBAN.md](../../docs/agent/KANBAN.md) and the active card’s `status` before acting.

## On every user request

1. **Locate or create** a card under `.devtool/features/` (default new → `triage/`).
2. **Read** `status` in frontmatter — that column is the **only** phase you execute this turn unless the user explicitly overrides.
3. **Do not write product code** until the card is in **`ready`** or **`in-progress`** (and `in-progress` only after passing the Ready gate).
4. **Advance the card** when the phase exit criteria are met (move on board or run `python scripts/sync_kanban_folders.py` after editing `status`).
5. Report: **current column**, **what you did**, **exit criteria met?**, **next column**.

## Column → agent obligations

| Column | You do | Exit → next |
|--------|--------|-------------|
| **triage** | Clarify intent; link roadmap slice; name PR/slice | Scope bounded → **spec** |
| **spec** | Draft `docs/superpowers/specs/NNN-…-design.md` (`brainstorming`) | Draft complete → stay for review |
| **spec** (review) | Self-review / `grill-me`; lock decisions; mark spec **approved** in doc | Spec approved → **plan** |
| **plan** | Draft `docs/superpowers/plans/NNN-…-….md` (`writing-plans`) | Draft complete → review |
| **plan** (review) | Plan vs spec; fix gaps; mark plan **approved** | Plan approved → **todo** |
| **todo** | Break work into **priority-ordered** tasks on the card (checklist); no implementation | Priorities set → **scheduled** |
| **scheduled** | Select **one** next task; confirm spec+plan links on card | Task queued → **ready** (or stay if more scheduling passes) |
| **ready** | Verify spec ↔ plan ↔ acceptance; branch name; `files_allowed` mental model | Gate pass → **in-progress** |
| **in-progress** | Implement (`executing-plans` / minimal diff); targeted tests | Implementation complete → **review** |
| **review** | Code review, PR, verification matrix | Green + merged → **done** |
| **blocked** | Report blocker only; no scope creep | User/unblock → prior column |
| **done** | Update `current_query.md`, roadmap changelog; close card | — |

## Hard gates

- **No `src/` or `web/` product changes** in `triage`, `spec`, `plan`, or `todo`.
- **`scheduled`**: at most **one** active “next task” per card body; do not start coding.
- **`ready`**: card must link approved spec + approved plan paths; agent prints a 3-line gate checklist before **in-progress**.
- **`in-progress` → `review`**: tests run or explain why not.
- Roadmap PRs: also follow [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md); kanban column wins over informal “just implement” unless user approves skipping gates.

## Artifacts on the card

Keep on the card markdown body:

- Links to spec, plan, branch, roadmap
- **Todo** section: numbered priority list
- **Scheduled** section: which task is active
- **Ready** checklist: spec approved ✓ plan approved ✓ scope match ✓

## Non-roadmap work

Small tickets in `BACKLOG.yml` still get a kanban card (label `backlog`) or reuse an existing card; same column rules apply.
